# Paste into the Komodo Stack "Environment" field.
# [[NAME]] interpolates a Komodo Variable — no values live in this repo.
#
# GHOST_DB_PASSWORD must be marked Secret in Komodo. The same value is consumed by
# both services: it provisions the MySQL user and authenticates Ghost's connection,
# so they cannot drift apart. Note there is no root password to store — ghost-db
# runs with MYSQL_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD, so mysqldump runs as the ghost user.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN must be marked Secret. On its own it is enough to run a
# connector for this tunnel, so treat it like a private key rather than a config
# value. Rotate it from Zero Trust > Networks > Tunnels if it ever leaks.
#
# GHOST_DOMAIN is referenced rather than written out. The value is not a secret —
# the site is public — but this repo is public too, and there is no reason to hand
# anyone a mapping from "kevinkorte/homelab" to the blog it runs. Keeping it in
# Komodo breaks that link without pretending the domain itself is hidden.
#
# Set it as a plain Komodo Variable (Secret flag optional; it only hides the value
# in the UI). Hostname only: no scheme, no trailing slash, no www.
GHOST_DOMAIN=[[GHOST_DOMAIN]]
GHOST_DB_PASSWORD=[[GHOST_DB_PASSWORD]]
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=[[CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN]]
